{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RECENT DISTRIBUTION (20 most recent completed runs queried 2026-08-14): 15 were full routes with a macOS job >1,000s. Their observed mean wall was 2,117.8s (35m18s), including the two pre-cancellation-fix same-change queue outliers. Removing only those two proven obsolete queue cases leaves 13 full routes averaging 1,945.3s (32m25s). This confirms the residual problem is not only the 57m anecdote: ordinary runs remain about 2m25s above the 30-minute upper target on average. The sample spans patchsets on older bases as well as current code, so use the first post-4cbaa/18f current-base organic runs as the decision-quality post-remediation series; do not claim the 32m25s value as a clean treatment estimate."},"env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786747634057659001,"uuid":"adbdc3ab-1d2b-4699-be30-c9e3664c2be2"}